From: Azathothas <ajamx101@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 07:31:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] A refusal of PODNET_POLICY gives the step of the policy,
 not of a connect hop

GitHub #727. The second line of the error of a refusal of the egress
policy was the step of a failed connect hop (check the host, the port,
--proxy). The refusal comes before any connect, so that step is false.

- src/policy/said.rs reads the refusal in the chain: the typed Refused
  first, then the words of the reason (a layer that keeps only the text:
  pod-ws, the first error of bench). It gives the rule (or the default),
  and the variable and the file that gave the policy, with
  podnet rules check FILE.
- report::error_line gives that line before each other hint.
- connect: the lead of a refused remote is "the egress policy refuses
  the remote", not "does not answer".
- egress::dial, dial_direct, dial_addrs, permit_fault and permit_failure
  keep the typed Refused in the chain.
- docs/host-runtime.md says the two lines.

Tests: policy::said::tests::each_shape_of_a_refusal_gives_the_step_of_the_policy,
each_refusal_reads_back_as_its_rule, the_hint_names_the_file_of_the_rules;
egress_refusal a_refusal_gives_the_step_of_the_policy_in_each_command
(bench direct, bench with --proxy, connect).
